{"id":1136,"date":"2015-03-12T08:56:04","date_gmt":"2015-03-12T08:56:04","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/?page_id=1136"},"modified":"2016-09-22T11:22:02","modified_gmt":"2016-09-22T11:22:02","slug":"cambridge2015","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/cambridge2015\/","title":{"rendered":"Cambridge 2015"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>News:<\/strong><\/span>\u00a0<span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Best paper prize<\/span> winners are\u00a0<strong>Elvira Mitraka, Andra Waagmeester, Sebastian Burgstaller-Muehlbacher, Lynn M. Schriml, Andrew I. Su and Benjamin M. Good<\/strong> with <a href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/10\/SWAT4LS_2015_paper_38.pdf\">Wikidata: A platform for data integration and dissemination for the life sciences and beyond<\/a><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Best poster prize<\/span>\u00a0winners are\u00a0<strong>Thanos Stavropoulos, Georgios Meditskos and Ioannis Kompatsiaris<\/strong> with\u00a0Dem@Care: Ambient Sensing and Intelligent Decision Support for the Care of Dementia\u00a0(prize sponsored by\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.factbio.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FactBio<\/a>)<\/p>\n<p>Runner up for best poster prize are\u00a0Bas Stringer, Albert Mero\u00f1o-Pe\u00f1uela, Antonis Loizou, Sanne Abeln and Jaap Heringa with \u00a0SCRY: Enabling quantitative reasoning in SPARQL queries<\/p>\n<p>and\u00a0Daniel Teixeira, Alain Gateau, Olivier Evalet, Frederic Nikitin, Jerven Bolleman, Monique Zahn, Pascale Gaudet, Lydie Lane, Amos Bairoch and Pierre-Andre Michel with SPARQL playground.<\/p>\n<p>The next SWAT4LS will be held in Cambridge, UK, 7-10th December 2015 and will be a full conference for the first time. SWAT4LS 2015 will comprise a tutorials day (7th), main conference (8th and 9th), and a Hackathon day (10th). Tutorials and the conference itself will be held in Clare College Conferencing, Cambridge and the Hackathon will be at the European Bioinformatics Institute, Hinxton, Cambridge.<\/p>\n<p>The 2015 SWAT4LS conference is the seventh meeting in the series and will provide the same open, vibrant and well-organised environment that has previously brought together researchers, developers, and users, from many fields to discuss goals, current limits and real experiences in the use of Semantic Web technologies in health care and the life sciences.<\/p>\n<h2>Key dates<\/h2>\n<p><del>&#8211; Abstract and paper submission\u00a0&#8211;\u00a0call for papers now out!<\/del><br \/>\n&#8211; <del>Expression of interest for tutorials 24th August<\/del><br \/>\n<del>&#8211; Abstract submission 7th September<\/del><br \/>\n<del>&#8211; Full Paper submission 15th September (Midnight UK)<\/del><br \/>\n<del>&#8211; Poster abstracts 1st October<\/del><br \/>\n<del>&#8211; Notification of acceptance 19th October<\/del><\/p>\n<p>Registration is now closed for this event.<\/p>\n<p>-Tutorials 7th December,\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/clareconferencing.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Clare College\u00a0Conferencing<\/a>, Cambridge University<br \/>\n-Conference 8th-9th December\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/clareconferencing.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Clare College\u00a0Conferencing<\/a>, Cambridge University<br \/>\n-Hackathon 10th December\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.ebi.ac.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">European Bioinformatics Institute<\/a>, Cambridge<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<h6>Cambridge Logo credit:\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.freepik.com\/free-vector\/cambridge-university-skyline_761432.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Derived from Freepik<\/a><\/h6>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>News:\u00a0Best paper prize winners are\u00a0Elvira Mitraka, Andra Waagmeester, Sebastian Burgstaller-Muehlbacher, Lynn M. Schriml, Andrew I. Su and Benjamin M. Good with Wikidata: A platform for data integration and dissemination for the life sciences and beyond Best poster prize\u00a0winners are\u00a0Thanos Stavropoulos, &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/cambridge2015\/\">Continue reading <span class=\"meta-nav\">&rarr;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1853,"parent":219,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-1136","page","type-page","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/1136","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=1136"}],"version-history":[{"count":42,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/1136\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1902,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/1136\/revisions\/1902"}],"up":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/219"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1853"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1136"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}